<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A line offer in the Italian profile of South Tyrol (IT-ITH1), shaped as the
  national access point publishes it: one document, identifiers of the form
  IT:ITH1:<class>:<code>:, every name with its language — a stop named in
  Italian, German and Ladin, a stop named in one language only with a second
  name leaving out its town —, stop places stating their submodes, a bus line
  whose pattern names its line through a route view and a train whose pattern
  names only its route, the route naming the line; a calendar of UIC day bits
  named through an OperatingPeriodRef, and the train's number for
  advertisement in the timetable frame. Written for netex-rs's tests
  (MIT OR Apache-2.0); places, lines, numbers and times are invented.
-->
